Slow Slow Slow - this game is somewhat annoying to review on here as there is no midle ground, its either reccomend or don't and to be honest, after completing it i am a little unsure.
The game it's self is quite good for the most part with an ok story and not too bad voice acting, that being said - it's very slow going and extremly repetative throughout, which in the end leaves you with so many unasnwered questions, makes you wonder why you just spent so much time clearing it.
if you want a good story though and don't mind the fact that it relies on repertition, then by all means give it a go - only if it's on sale though :)

Forget the general critics from "God of♥♥♥♥♥♥♥quot; and "Symphony of the Night" fans (the majority of them just played SOTN and dont really knows about Castlevania games at all) this is a deep very well made fan service.
Rule of the tumb: if you liked the 1st Castlevania: Lords of Shadow this game is a "Instabuy"
***Edited at 09/13/14 to review the DLC Revelations.***
PROS:
- Improved combat and movement mechanics making this even more solid;
- Awesome graphics and immersive scenarios (combine several aspects of Vampire lore with Castlevania's elements);
- Free movement camera;
- Lots of extra content including: 400 pages of design artwork (seems much but it is easy to have those collected during the game - I've completed mine in the 1st run), Challenges and Lore
- Fantastic follow up history;
- About 14~17 hours long (if you're a completionist and like achievements you would mostly at least double that time);
- On LOS1 the platforming wasn't really great and you finished get killed by bad jumping several times. That was corrected!
CONS:
- Although stealth isn't that bad as people say (in reality just a puzzle) it is so easy that doesn't adds any value to the gameplay at all;
- In 17 hours -my 1st run- I didnt spend no more than 30 minutes with ALL puzzles (including stealth) which means that the puzzles are super easy. The LOS1 puzzles were waaaaay more fun;
- Voice acting, for Gabriel Belmont, should be better. During LOS1 it was "Fair" for a Brotherhood templar but it is not enough for Dracula;
DLC Revelations:
The level of disappointment provided by this one is only compared to Oblivion Horse Armor.
Add 2 hours of gamplay with an incredible weak plot.
Do a favor to yourself and skip this one.

