I was playing for quite a while Starbound and I noticed some things, so here's my opinion about game:
Pros:
+Nice, calm music;
+Smooth gameplay on even a non-gaming laptop;
+SPAAAAAACE (haha ok I love space so deal with it);
+Game is pleasant to play (except when game becomes a bit of a b!tch after you die in game for first time);
Cons:
-No smooth transition between different songs in game;
-Bit harsh for a newbie;
-Could be more of character customisation (merp don't blame meh, I love fully customising some in-game charaters);
-Game is a little too harsh on player when it comes to player trying to get back it's items after he/she dies (several times I had to spend a lot of time (and in game I died repeatedly too) while just trying to get my items back and that really annoyed me);
-Bit boring intro after you have seen it already;
Sure, my review may seem like there are more negative things than good ones - but in reality, I just pointed out what might be improved. All in all the game is pleasant to play, music of game is really good and I do recommend to play this game. After all, if you like Terraria, this game is similar to Terraria but it is more in space theme, and if you like such combo definitelly give it a try.

